fix-zgen-2phase-out-z2: marshal outZ2 as the second response parameter of TPM2_ZGen_2Phase

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 3, TPM2_ZGen_2Phase, Table "TPM2_ZGen_2Phase
Response"): "TPM2B_ECC_POINT outZ1 | X and Y coordinates of the computed value
(scheme dependent); TPM2B_ECC_POINT outZ2 | X and Y coordinates of the second
computed value (scheme dependent)"; "For TPM_ALG_ECDH outZ1 will be Zs and
outZ2 will be Ze".

The dispatch table of TPM2_ZGen_2Phase (CommandDispatch.inl) lists outZ1 for
both response parameters, so the response repeats outZ1 (Zs) instead of
outZ2: TPM_ALG_ECDH never returns Ze, and TPM_ALG_ECMQV/TPM_ALG_SM2 return Z
twice instead of Z and an Empty Point. The patch marshals outZ2 as the second
parameter.

diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
@@ -2290,7 +2290,9 @@ MAKE_DISPATCH_TABLE(
     MAKE_DISPATCH_SEPARATOR(START_OUTPUT_PARAMETERS),
     // Response output parameters
     MAKE_OUTPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPM2B_ECC_POINT, outZ1),
-    MAKE_OUTPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPM2B_ECC_POINT, outZ1),
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // Part 3, TPM2_ZGen_2Phase Response: the second parameter is outZ2.
+    MAKE_OUTPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPM2B_ECC_POINT, outZ2),
 );
 #undef CURRENT_TPM_COMMAND
 #endif  // CC_ZGen_2Phase
